  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201C;Raspberries for development&#x201D; A solid extension plan, Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The existing raspberry farm in Tanzania cultivates raspberries and strawberries for the European market for many years. There is a lot of demand for these so-called super fruits because of their nutritional and anti-oxidants. With co-financing from DGGF and Rabobank, the entrepreneur is able to expand the nursery with 45 ha.The company will invest in a cooling facility and the latest farming techniques. The investment creates 200 jobs for permanent employees and 300 seasonal jobs for employees. All employees receive a good salary and training opportunities. The investment results in an efficiency improvement of 30% per hectare and thereby contribute to the strengthening of local manufacturing strength.</narrative>
  </description>
